<p>What the whole site shares (its email, its forms, its spam protection and more) is set once in <strong>Theme Settings</strong>, in the left menu. Change it there and every page follows.</p>
{{ shot( 'theme-settings', 'Theme Settings: every page in the sidebar, its tabs, and Save changes.' ) }}

<h3>Find your way around</h3>
<ol class="guide-steps">
	<li>Click <a href="{{ go.app }}"><strong>Theme Settings</strong></a> in the left menu.</li>
	<li>The sidebar lists every page, in groups. Click one to open it: its title and what it is for are at the top.</li>
	<li>Most pages are split into <strong>tabs</strong>. Each tab holds part of the page; nothing is lost when you switch tabs.</li>
	<li>Click <strong>Save changes</strong> when you are done. Until you do, nothing is kept.</li>
</ol>

<h3>Who sees what</h3>
<p>You only see the pages your account may use. Editors usually see the content pages (a list page's banner and text, for example) and this guide; administrators see everything.</p>
